#. engine/messages/decoders_agree.py (ticket 10): the decoder cross-check's codes.
msgid "engine.decoders_agree.disagree"
msgstr "The two readers found different contents in this file: {only_first, plural, one {# item} other {# items}} only the first found, {only_second, plural, one {# item} other {# items}} only the second found, and different counts for {kinds, plural, one {# kind of item} other {# kinds of item}} and on {layers, plural, one {# layer} other {# layers}}. It is held, so nothing from it reaches the sheet list while it may be misread."

msgid "engine.decoders_agree.not_installed"
msgstr "This file was read once, not twice: the second reader is not installed here. It is held until it can be checked; mark it for Vextrus."

msgid "engine.decoders_agree.not_pinned"
msgstr "This file was read once, not twice: the second reader installed here is not the version Vextrus tested, so it was not used. It is held until it can be checked; mark it for Vextrus."

msgid "engine.decoders_agree.too_many"
msgstr "This file was read once, not twice: it holds more than {limit, number} items, more than the second reader's check takes. It is held until it can be checked; mark it for Vextrus."
